entityDescription:
VOLTA pioneers a groundbreaking technology enabling ZERO-VOLUME ENERGY STORAGE: Volta Structural Batteries (VSB). Our state-of-the-art multifunctional batteries serve as structural frames for spacecraft, aircrafts and trucks and virtually any transport vehicles, seamlessly integrating energy storage capabilities with their revolutionary architecture and constituent materials. VSB maximizes storable energy, power and, consequently, range within a given system without compromising the mass or volume required for passengers or cargo transport.
This groundbreaking advancement allows spacecraft ranging from 3U CubeSats to large 500+ Kg platforms to allocate 80% to 100% of the original battery pack volume to additional payload, resulting in a 40% reduction in the original battery pack mass and a 2X to 5X increase in available power.

Volta's architecture incorporates state of the art sodium-ion chemistry, the combination of this chemistry with the innovative design results in a highly advanced product with market competitive features such as:
&middot; Higher overall system energy density;
&middot; Fast charging: full charge in less than 15 minutes;
&middot; High power density: maximum power output for demanding applications;
&middot; High cycling and very long battery life, comparable with that of the systems in which it is integrated;
&middot; High mechanical strength and stiffness: properties typical of advanced sandwich composites;
&middot; High safety: robust safety features, even in cases of severe damage.
&middot; High customization: panels of different shapes, sizes and thicknesses can be made according to mechanical and electrochemical requirements, and different materials can also be used for the outer layers, such as high-performance composite materials for aerospace applications or metal and plastic materials for more low-cost applications. 
Volta's solution is also engineered to be produced on a large scale at low cost due to the possibility of using existing production techniques and abundant materials, and with a manageable supply chain even at the national/European level.
